{
  "_comment": "What each `derived` condition looks like in real code. Two kinds of evidence: a dependency named in a manifest, and a pattern in the app's own source. Source matters because several of these are reachable from a standard library with no dependency at all - Python's xml.etree and Java's JAXB are XML parsers nothing declares - so a dependency-only scan answering `false` would be the same class of wrong statement as the inherited reasons this replaced. Matching is case-insensitive substring: it over-matches rather than under-matches, and over-matching makes a condition true, which only ever adds requirements.",
